    "vo-roots",
    "vo-word"
  ],
  "figureArchetype": "GeneralFigure",
  "practice": null,
  "lesson": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "Greek gave English its words for who is in charge. <b>-cracy</b> (also <b>-crat</b>) means “rule” or “power”: <i>democracy</i> is rule by the people (<i>dem</i>, people). <b>-archy</b> (also <b>-arch</b>) means “rule” or “chief”: a <i>monarchy</i> is ruled by one (<i>mon</i>, one). And <b>auto-</b> means “self”: an <i>automatic</i> door opens by itself."
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-scene",
        "opts": {
          "scene": {
            "bg": "throne",
            "cast": [
              {
                "who": "pip",
                "x": 40,
                "pose": "point",
                "wear": [
                  "crown"
                ],
                "mood": "proud",
                "face": "right",
                "say": "I decide!"
              },
              {
                "who": "sami",
                "x": 76,
                "pose": "shrug",
                "mood": "confused",
                "face": "left"
              }
            ],
            "labels": [
              {
                "text": "AUTO-CRAT: rules alone",
                "x": 50,
                "y": 92
              }
            ],
            "alt": "A boy in a crown points and declares that he alone decides, while another boy shrugs."
          }
        },
        "cap": "A boy in a crown points and declares that he alone decides, while another boy shrugs."
      },
      {
        "t": "key",
        "html": "<b>-cracy</b>, <b>-crat</b> = <b>rule, power</b>. <b>-archy</b>, <b>-arch</b> = <b>rule, chief, first</b>. <b>auto-</b> = <b>self</b>."
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "Put a word for “who” in front and you name a kind of rule. <b>autocrat</b>: a self-ruler, one person with total power. <b>oligarchy</b>: rule by a few (<i>olig</i>, few). <b>anarchy</b>: no ruler at all (<i>an-</i>, without). <b>bureaucracy</b>: rule by offices (<i>bureau</i>, French for desk or office)."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "The parts and their words"
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "roots": [
            "cracy",
            "archy"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "Words on the list built on -cracy and -archy."
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "root": "auto"
        },
        "cap": "auto- (self)."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "Words taken apart"
      },
      {
        "t": "table",
        "head": [
          "Word and meaning",
          "Parts, and what they say"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "<b>autocrat</b><br>a ruler with total power",
            "<b>auto-</b> <i>self</i> + <b>crat</b> <i>ruler</i><br>→ “a self-ruler”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>autonomy</b><br>self-government; independence",
            "<b>auto-</b> <i>self</i> + nom <i>law</i> + -y<br>→ “self-law (making one’s own rules)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>bureaucracy</b><br>government by many officials and rules",
            "bureau <i>office, desk</i> + <b>-cracy</b> <i>rule</i><br>→ “rule by offices”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>anarchy</b><br>absence of government; disorder",
            "an- <i>without</i> + <b>arch</b> <i>ruler</i> + -y<br>→ “without a ruler”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>oligarchy</b><br>rule by a small group",
            "olig <i>few</i> + <b>-archy</b> <i>rule</i><br>→ “rule by a few”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>hierarchy</b><br>a system ranking people or things one above another",
            "hier <i>sacred</i> + <b>-archy</b> <i>rule</i><br>→ “sacred rule (ranks of priests, then any ranking)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b><i>monarchy</i></b><br>a country ruled by a king or queen",
            "mon- <i>one</i> + <b>-archy</b> <i>rule</i><br>→ “rule by one”"
          ],
          [
            "<b><i>democracy</i></b><br>government by the people, usually through elected leaders",
            "demo <i>people</i> + <b>-cracy</b> <i>rule</i><br>→ “rule by the people”"
          ]
        ],
        "cap": "Each word, what it means now, and its parts. Words in italics are familiar words that are not on the list."
      },
      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "Use the parts",
        "q": "In the old city, a handful of rich families made every decision. Was it a democracy, a monarchy or an <b>oligarchy</b>?",
        "steps": [
          "<b>democracy</b>: <i>demo</i> (people) + <i>-cracy</i>: rule by the people. Not this one.",
          "<b>monarchy</b>: <i>mon</i> (one) + <i>-archy</i>: rule by one. Not this one either.",
          "<b>oligarchy</b>: <i>olig</i> (few) + <i>-archy</i>: rule by a few. A handful of families is a few."
        ],
        "a": "An oligarchy."
      },
