      {
        "t": "mistake",
        "html": "<b>arch</b> does not always mean rule. It can also mean “chief” or “first”: an <i>archenemy</i> is a chief enemy, and an <i>archetype</i> is a first model that others copy. And a <b>hierarchy</b> is now any ranking from top to bottom, not just one run by priests."
